lines+=['','Default AM SVG totals have median4.512s versus main4.680s; balanced4.791s versus main4.749s. Three-repeat ranges overlap, so no formal speed win is claimed. The targeted Node stress cases below show costs that this corpus total hides.','','## Label outcomes and public meaning','','All AM layout arms share the same measured parser outcomes, including per-file callback order and repeated-title ordinals: [exact comparison](fidelity-callback-equality.json). Current/main each have2,863 scored passes,355 known nonpasses and187 unassessed callbacks. Known nonpasses include132 actual failures,116 oracle-verified refusals and107 confirmed absent concepts. These are inherited limitations, not a claim of complete Mermaid compatibility.','','Pele has3,204 passes,183 known nonpasses and18 unknowns over the same3,405 callbacks. Mermaid’s reference control has3,405 passes. ZM has1,217 passes,1,474 known nonpasses and714 unknowns; new unbound families receive no pass credit. BM has237 passes,3,167 known nonpasses and one unknown; this broad corpus includes many families outside its narrower parser.','','Current/main SVG labels:126 correct /127, one renderer refusal. Historical Native:124 correct /127, three refusals. Pele:125 correct, one unknown and one refusal; its unknown could tie AM. The common AM refusal is the frozen regression with a bare `subgraph` and no id/title. It was not silently removed. Native additionally refuses the eight-retry self-loop input for local loop-attachment capacity and a USER→PROJECT ER corridor. Those two current-versus-Native differences already exist on main and are not new PR621 gains.','','## Actual retained SVG geometry','','The unchanged Trident observer assessed72 flowchart inputs per configuration where possible. Every pair below uses identical case IDs and only a metric completely assessed on both sides. Excluded/capped rows and reasons remain in the raw observer output; no unknown is zero. Counts use Trident’s emitted-SVG policy, not a new aesthetics weighting.','','| Pair (AM balanced on left) | Common crossing cases | AM crossings | Peer crossings | AM lower / peer lower / equal |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---|']
