lines+=['','## Browser memory and actual compressed assets, all systems','','One additional full1,342-case SVG pass per configuration reuses the unchanged Trident browser host, renderer call and mechanical admission, without a timing ranking. Every row completed collection. [All samples, output failures and resource hashes](browser-resources/results.json). RSS is a sampled sum over that Chromium instance’s process tree, so shared pages may be counted more than once; it is not standalone library RSS. JS heap excludes WASM/external/GPU memory. Post-GC heap is measured after the full population; no forced GC occurs during it. This single pass is not a calibrated memory comparison, and rejected inputs impose different work.','','Gzip is actual level9 compression of each exact unique executable/resource body; Brotli is quality11. Inlined entry bytes are explicitly charged, so an inline script is never a zero-byte delivery claim. Requested assets and provided entries are separate fields in the raw records. These are all-family Trident adapter artifacts, not AM’s production flow-only lazy closure or a hosted-site deployment.','','| Configuration | Raw returns /1342 | Sampled browser-tree RSS MiB | Peak observed JS heap MiB | Post-GC JS heap MiB | Gzip bytes | Brotli bytes | Unique assets |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for x in resources:
 lines.append('| '+' | '.join([labels.get(x['id'],x['id']),str(x['completed']),f"{x['peakSampledBrowserTreeRssKiB']/1024:.2f}",f"{x['peakObservedJsHeapBytes']/1048576:.2f}",f"{x.get('afterGcHeap',{}).get('usedSize',0)/1048576:.2f}",f"{x['compressedUniqueAssetTotals']['gzip']:,}",f"{x['compressedUniqueAssetTotals']['brotli']:,}",str(x['compressedUniqueAssetTotals']['files'])])+' |')
lines+=['','Current default’s Trident artifact is1,129,682gzip bytes versus main1,127,266: **+2,416**, with one provided bundle each. Balanced adds the same2,416gzip bytes. The old Native/ELK.js Trident artifacts both retain their shared monolithic package closure; they do not describe Native-only production lazy downloads. Pele’s275,154gzip bytes and lower observed browser heap are meaningful observations at its public SVG boundary, alongside its32 reference-accepted render misses. They do not establish equivalence to AM’s full receipt/certification API.','','### npm archive, main versus PR','','| Artifact | Archive bytes | Unpacked regular-file bytes | Regular files | SHA256 |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---|']
pack=[]
for arm in ['main','current']:
 f=next((p/(arm+'-archive')).glob('*.tgz'));members=tarfile.open(f).getmembers();n=sum(m.isfile() for m in members);size=sum(m.size for m in members if m.isfile());pack.append({'arm':arm,'archiveBytes':f.stat().st_size,'unpackedBytes':size,'files':n,'sha256':hashlib.sha256(f.read_bytes()).hexdigest()});x=pack[-1];lines.append(f"| {arm} | {x['archiveBytes']:,} | {size:,} | {n} | `{x['sha256']}` |")
(p/'package-sizes.json').write_text(json.dumps(pack,indent=2));lines+=['','The package archive adds11,040bytes versus main; file count stays270. These are package archives, not the transitive installed production-dependency closure. Current’s fresh archive has exactly the same270 payloads/modes as the prior tested6d archive; [payload identity](current-archive-payload-identity.json). No source rebuild improvement is inferred from archive-envelope bytes. Existing unchanged lazy/actual-Chromium payload budgets passed local checks on this exact source head; no cap was raised and no new CI run is claimed here.','','## Merge reassessment','','The earlier small-example statement that Pele “has more crossings” should not be generalized. The complete common crossing population ties AM/Pele, and Pele’s full Trident score range is above AM’s. Pele is also much faster on its observed public SVG corpus totals and has a smaller measured benchmark artifact, while AM renders more inputs. Those are separate facts, not an equal-work global speed ranking.','','PR621 remains a defensible scoped readability/traceability repair with the owner-accepted costs: its owning regressions are red→green, prior exact-head local checks pass, no full-corpus semantic/structure regression was observed, and the targeted wallet/ordering gains remain demonstrated at the unchanged head. The broad headline score does not improve, and optional balanced stress costs are substantial. If the criterion were “no slower than main on every case” or “better than Pele on all metrics,” the evidence does not meet it. No fresh approval question is introduced for already accepted costs.','','The exact-head existing local verification remains17,073 unit passes /78 skips /zero failures,900 focused tests, build/types/lint and local quality/payload checks. Those were run on21November; this task did not rerun unchanged CI. Remote workflow runs remain empty as requested. The PR stays draft and unmerged.','','Issue619 stays open: cyclic19 and seed139 crossing/paint gaps, different-rank arrival behavior outside the local predicate, and incomplete common glyph/ink observation remain. The next performance intervention should profile the extra balanced candidate’s producer, route/occurrence validation and paint work before removing repeated work at its shared owner. The separate long-edge port-rank/position allocation proposal has not been implemented or credited.','','## Preserved failures and reproducibility','','- Frozen-catalog timestamp refusal, sandbox Bun pipe failure, unsupported peer terminal selection, read-only npm cache failure and their actual recoveries are retained in the command/status logs. No failed collector was relabelled successful.','- All native/render/admission failures, partial observations and observer cap reasons remain in the raw archives. Original invalid Event edits and successful corrections are both retained. Initial fully unreviewed peer Fidelity scores remain in `scores-initial-unreviewed.json`.','- The first model-review catalog selected older0.4/5.14 pins; those preparations remain separate. The actual comparisons use reviewed0.5 a5be33/5.17 versus measured0.6/5.18. Bun’s `node:v8` serialization shim produced the model files; the attempted Node decoder rejected that format. Read them using Bun1.4.4, as the successful comparison did.','- No production code, default, version, cap, golden or dependency changed. No new PR, issue, merge, release or remote CI was requested.','','Start from Trident release`ceb42...`, apply `trident-adapters-vs-release.patch`, and install its pinned dependencies per Trident’s README. Place that checkout at `harness/` beside the retained scripts. The frozen catalogs, prepared artifact manifests, exact archive identities, raw commands in `collection*-status.json`, original input revisions and every source/output digest bind this report. Installation roots in raw jobs are the actual measured paths and must be rebound to verified identical artifacts to reproduce elsewhere. `reduce-reviewed.ts` uses only canonical Trident report/merge/scoring helpers; `compare-observations.py` sums only common fully assessed existing metric values. `browser-resources.ts` is a resource observer around the existing host/call, not a new scorer.','','Raw directories are archived separately in the evidence packet to avoid installing packages or committing evidence into the PR’s source diff. The packet manifest records each published file’s hash; install trees and package bundles are not included. Prior captioned visual evidence stays at its immutable links.','']
(p/'REPORT.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines));print('report bytes',len((p/'REPORT.md').read_bytes()),'package',pack)
